70 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 43 0 R
/E (2. Scaling Global Capability Centres \(GCCs\) and Enhancing Ease of Business)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
71 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 43 0 R
/E (India currently hosts over 1,800 GCCs, making it a global hub for high-value innovation. To maintain this edge, there is a strong demand for a concessional tax regime for newly established or expanding GCCs, potentially mirroring the 15% rate previously offered to manufacturing units. Operational friction remains a concern; specifically, the industry seeks clarity on cross-border secondment arrangements. Currently, reimbursements for seconded staff often trigger double withholding under Sections 192 and 195, leading to prolonged litigation. A clarification that salary already subject to withholding under Section 192 should not be taxed again under Section 195 would significantly improve the Ease of Doing Business. Additionally, rationalizing Safe Harbour margins to reflect actual business realities \(suggested reduction to 14-15%\) would encourage more GCCs to opt for certainty over litigation.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
