89 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 44 0 R
/E (Foreign investors require a roadmap for complex provisions like Significant Economic Presence \(SEP\). While thresholds have been notified, the lack of final profit attribution rules creates uncertainty for non-residents estimating their Indian tax liability. Industry advocates for clear rules using objective parameters like user base or revenue contribution. Furthermore, there is a request to ensure that retrospective notifications defining treaty terms do not lead to unintended tax consequences or the reopening of concluded assessments.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
90 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 44 0 R
/E (5. Simplifying Capital Gains Taxation)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
91 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 44 0 R
/E (The reform of the capital gains regime remains a top priority to enhance market depth. Expectations include reducing the holding period for business "undertakings" from 36 months to 24 months to qualify for long-term status, aligning it with other capital assets. Investors also seek clarity on the taxation of contingent consideration, recommending that such gains be chargeable only in the year they are crystallized rather than the year of transfer. For foreign investors, exempting genuine transactions involving frequently traded listed shares acquired off the stock exchange from anti-abuse provisions would support legitimate M&A activities.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
92 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
